From 44488bb4be0130bc7d925c4134bc594ebeca3ce4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: warelik <warelik@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 11:28:27 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 03/12] Add compact threads sidebar and halve its minimum width

Each sidebar thread takes two lines even when its only metadata is a
timestamp, so few threads fit on screen. With
agent.threads_sidebar.compact a thread is one row at the tab bar
height, and hovering it trades the title for the metadata and actions.
Project group headers take the same height, and so does the "No threads
yet" row of an empty group; the search header keeps only the input;
Escape still clears the query. The setting defaults to false, which
keeps the two-line rows.

The minimum width of the threads sidebar drops from 200 to 100 pixels
for every user. One-line rows stay readable that narrow, so the sidebar
can be dragged narrower and leave more room for the editor. The clamp
also applies to agent.threads_sidebar.default_width, so its schema
range and documentation now start at 100.

AgentSettings::from_settings deserializes threads_sidebar.compact with
unwrap_or(false), accompanied by regression test coverage ensuring safe
fallback to stock defaults when the compact setting is omitted.
